<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3942" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Āsōpis</span></b> ,
		ĭdis, f. (<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>gen.</i> Gr. Asopidos, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 7,
				616</span></i>; acc. Gr Asopida, <i><span class="en">id. ib. 6,
				113</span></i>), = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀσωπίς</span>.
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Daughter of Asopus</i>, i. e. <i>Ægina</i>, <i>the mother of
				Æacus by Jupiter</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 6,
				113</span></i>; <i><span class="en">7, 616</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>His daughter Evadne</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. Am. 3,
				6, 41</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A name of the island Eubœa</i> (after
			Eubœa, the third daughter of Asopus), <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 12,
				21, § 64</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>IV.</b>
			Adj. for <i>Bœotian</i> (v
			Asopus), <i><span class="en">Stat. Th. 4, 370</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
